1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:07,000
Some of my strongest childhood memories may seem like small things to others.

2
00:00:07,000 --> 00:00:14,000
My father's office was close to our home, and I would insist on going with him.

3
00:00:14,000 --> 00:00:21,000
He wouldn't say no. I would go with him, sit beside him, and watch him work.

4
00:00:21,000 --> 00:00:30,000
Ah, childhood! What I eagerly waited for was tea and donuts. Even now, I can remember the taste.

5
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:37,500
When he felt I was struggling at school, he helped and guided me. I don't remember him ever speaking to me harshly.

6
00:00:37,500 --> 00:00:43,500
He could notice what I was missing just by looking at me, and he would give me the attention I needed.

7
00:00:43,500 --> 00:00:53,500
His acts of care are engraved in my memory. I will never forget him washing my hands and feet, applying cream, and gently massaging them.

8
00:00:53,500 --> 00:01:01,500
The hardest times for me were when my father left for fieldwork. Sometimes I would hide in my bed and cry.

9
00:01:01,500 --> 00:01:08,000
But when he returned, I was so happy that it felt as if the whole world were mine.

10
00:01:08,000 --> 00:01:13,000
For me, my father means everything.

11
00:01:13,000 --> 00:01:25,000
In our community, we often focus on a mother's love and care. But for me, I found all of that in my father.
